{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Managing the Restaurant"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Hiring New People"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 5}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Express duty, advice, willingness, or intention to do something in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le05ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The First Conditional"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the First Conditional with If clauses to exchange opinions about possible outcomes in the present or in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the First Conditional to say it's possible that you will or will not do something. In that condition, something else may, may not, will or will not happen. The condition is in the present. The outcome is not in the present, but in the future.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Example</span>: <span class=\"italic\">If you focus more on our customers, they'll leave a larger tip.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The situation is dependent on meeting the condition. The outcome may happen as a result of that condition being met."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Structure: <span class=\"italic\">If + Present Simple, \u2026 will + verb \u2026</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">Will+verb \u2026 If+Present Simple</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you take a longer view of staffing, you will find motivated and talented employees who can provide good customer service and help you maintain profitability for the long term."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you give preference to someone with restaurant experience, they will understand the flexibility needed in scheduling, and will know how to contribute to a smooth and efficient work flow."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You will also get a lot of help in training if you use this method. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you ask the people you interview to respond to questions in each of these areas, you will develop a sense of the skill set you will get if you hire that person."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Modals for Duty or Obligation"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use a variety of modals to talk about duties and obligations, to express what someone is responsible for and to give strong advice and recommendations. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Let's look at the modals <span class=\"italic\">must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">have to</span>, <span class=\"italic\">have got to</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">should<span class=\"italic\">. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the modal <span class=\"italic\">must</span> when you decide for yourself what is necessary.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Example</span>: <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">must</span> show them I can live up to their expectations. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">have to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">have got to</span> before verbs that talk about necessity. </span>Have got to<span class=\"italic\"> is more casual. </span>Have to<span class=\"italic\"> implies that someone else imposed the necessity on you.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Examples</span>: <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">have to buckle down</span> Kristi, and get it done. </span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">I'<span class=\"strong\">ve got to work</span> systematically.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Should</span> is a modal you can use to give advice and to talk about duty.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Examples</span>: <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">should</span> make sure you meet these deadlines. </span>(advice)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">should</span> take this responsibility seriously. </span> (duty)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the following examples from the text:"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You have to consider that applicant seriously."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You must look for employees that can fit into the overall culture of your restaurant. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You have got to write down the types of skills you need in employees."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "take the long view"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to think about the effect that something will have in the future rather than what happens now"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If you take a longer view of staffing, you will find motivated and talented employees."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob07aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about who to hire. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hiring practice "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a particular way of finding people to employ "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You have got to establish some hiring practices to make sure you will have a qualified, professional staff."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob07aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to result in"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make something happen "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Evaluate whether nearby colleges or online job search sites have resulted in qualified employees."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob07aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to track"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to record the progress of something over time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You must track results of all of your recruitment sources."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob07aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "capacity "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone's job or position"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Try to find someone who has worked in several capacities."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob07aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": " to fit into "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be a part of "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You must look for employees that can fit into the overall culture of your restaurant."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob07aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Imagine that you have created your own company. Give your company a name."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Decide on 8-10 well-known people from the world of sports, politics, entertainment, science, history, business, and so on that you have to hire to help you in your company. You can assign them job titles if you want to be more creative (managers, regular employees, account manager, etc.)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present your \u201cstaff\u201d list in a group. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss your choices. Say who you chose and why."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In groups, choose 10 people to hire from everyone's staff list."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember to include everyone in the discussion and try to reach a compromise about who to \u201cfire\u201d and wh